{"_id":"68a736358ec3d8323af1dbb7","nodeId":"3pL0ARqk8uRNimopHSalW","roadmapSlug":"rust","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:32.844Z","description":"# Networking\n\nRust's `std::net` module provides networking primitives including `TcpStream`, `TcpListener`, `UdpSocket`, and address types. Built on BSD sockets, it offers low-level network operations for building networking applications. Higher-level crates like Tokio provide async networking capabilities.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"std::net","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/net/","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdc9c"},{"type":"official","title":"TcpListener","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/net/struct.TcpListener.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdc9d"},{"type":"official","title":"UdpSocket","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/net/struct.UdpSocket.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdc9e"},{"type":"official","title":"TcpStream","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/net/struct.TcpStream.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdc9f"},{"type":"article","title":"Networking Fundamentals in Rust","url":"https://medium.com/@murataslan1/networking-fundamentals-in-rust-525dcfbd5058","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdca0"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:07:02.070Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/rust/content/3pL0ARqk8uRNimopHSalW.md"}